.AVIATION...
(00Z TAFS)
Issued at 345 PM PST Mon Nov 23 2026

High confidence of VFR conditions until about 20Z tomorrow as rain
starts to move in with the cold front. Winds are light and variable
tonight out of the NE and shifting SE early tomorrow morning and
increasing. High confidence that ceilings will remain high, but
lowering ceilings are possible alongside rain showers tomorrow.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR conditions are likely to prevail through the majority of
the TAF period, but MVFR to IFR conditions are possible during rain
showers tomorrow. Prevailing winds are northeasterly, but will
quickly shift back out of the southeast by 04-05Z. High confidence
of wind speeds exceeding 10-15 kts with gusts up to 30 kts ahead of
the front. Highest wind speeds are highly likely to be during the
afternoon and evening hours.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...MRY and SNS seeing only a few high clouds right now. Winds at
MRY are light out of the W, but are expected to shift to SE later
tonight. Winds remain from the SE for SNS. Both sites have
chances of wind gusts up to 15-20KT tomorrow afternoon as the
front approaches. Rain arrives after 00Z and will be included in
the next TAF period.


